                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued November 2 at 1:23PM MST until November 2 at 8:00PM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "FFWFGZ\n\nThe National Weather Service in Flagstaff has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nCoconino County in north central Arizona...\nNavajo County in north central Arizona...\n\n* Until 800 PM MST Monday.\n\n* At 123 PM MST, the river gauge on the Little Colorado River at\nWinslow has risen above Major flood stage. Additional rises are\nforecast through late tonight, with flooding impacts to Ames Acres\nand Bushman Acres in Winslow. Flash flooding is already occurring.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...River gauge reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of the Little Colorado\nRiver.\n\n* For Little Colorado at Winslow:\nAt 1:00pm MST the stage was 25.1 feet.\nFlood Stage is 19.0 feet.\nForecast: A crest of 40.15 feet is expected at 3:00am MST Tuesday.\nImpacts:\nAt 25.0 feet: Levee is overtopped. Major flooding of portions of\nWinslow including Ames Acres and Bushman Acres.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nWinslow, Leupp, Birdsprings, Sunrise, Bushman Acres and Homolovi\nRuins State Park.\n\nThis includes the following highways...\nInterstate 40 between mile markers 254 and 258. Business Interstate\n40 between mile markers 256 and 257. State Route 87 between mile\nmarkers 346 and 347.\n\nThis includes the following recreation areas and campgrounds...\nHomolovi State Park Campground.\n\nThis includes the following creeks, washes and rivers...\nLittle Colorado River.",
                "instruction": "Be aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.\n\nStay away or be swept away! The banks of creeks and washes are\nunstable and unsafe during any flooding event.\n\nLow water crossings will become dangerous in heavy rain. Do not\nattempt to cross flooded roads. Find an alternate route.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
